---
import Section from './Section.astro';
// Reframed for a normal reader: the guardrail + validator become two plain
// "hard checks", with the fuller sequence in plain words below. Mechanism per
// INTELLIGENCE.md §3 (guardrail is checked before the citation check; both hard).
const steps = [
  {
    n: '1',
    title: 'Turns away off-limits questions',
    desc: 'Emergencies, diagnoses, medication, and mental-health crises go straight to a professional, before the model is even involved.',
    hard: false,
  },
  {
    n: '2',
    title: 'Reads only your real data',
    desc: 'Your recent numbers, trends, sleep, and the routines you logged — pulled from your own history, not assumed.',
    hard: false,
  },
  {
    n: '3',
    title: 'Finds the research that fits',
    desc: 'It pulls in the real research that matches your question, so the answer stands on evidence — not on a good guess.',
    hard: false,
  },
  {
    n: '4',
    title: 'Drafts an answer',
    desc: 'Using the lookups above, so it works from real numbers instead of a confident guess.',
    hard: false,
  },
  {
    n: '5',
    title: 'Check 1 — should it answer at all?',
    desc: 'Off-limits answers are stopped here even when they’re perfectly sourced. This runs first, on purpose.',
    hard: true,
  },
  {
    n: '6',
    title: 'Check 2 — is every claim backed?',
    desc: 'Each thing it tells you has to trace back to real research, worded to match how strong that evidence actually is.',
    hard: true,
  },
  {
    n: '7',
    title: 'Falls back honestly',
    desc: 'If it still can’t back the answer, you get “I can’t back that up” — never an invented one.',
    hard: false,
  },
];
---

<Section id="trust" labelledby="trust-h">
  <h2 id="trust-h" class="rise mt-4 max-w-2xl text-[clamp(1.9rem,4vw,3rem)]">
    Why it can’t lie to you.
  </h2>
  <p class="lede rise mt-6 max-w-2xl">
    Before an answer ever reaches your screen, it has to pass two hard checks. Neither one can be
    talked around, and the model can’t switch them off.
  </p>

  <div class="checks rise mt-10 max-w-3xl">
    <div class="check">
      <span class="check-n">Hard check 1</span>
      <p class="check-q">Is this an answer a health app should ever give?</p>
      <p class="check-d">
        Anything that crosses into medical territory — a diagnosis, a guess at how long you have to
        live, advice to skip sleep or meals — is refused outright. It doesn’t matter how good the
        sources are; some answers simply aren’t ours to give.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="check">
      <span class="check-n">Hard check 2</span>
      <p class="check-q">Can every claim be backed?</p>
      <p class="check-d">
        Everything it tells you has to trace back to real research you can read yourself, worded to
        match how strong that evidence is. Anything it can’t back up gets dropped — and if it can’t
        be fixed, you get an honest “I can’t back that up” instead.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="rise mt-10 max-w-3xl">
    <p class="eyebrow">The full path, in plain words</p>
    <ol class="flow mt-5">
      {
        steps.map((s) => (
          <li class="flow-step">
            <span class="flow-num">{s.n}</span>
            <div>
              <p class="flow-title">
                {s.title}
                {s.hard && <span class="hard">hard check</span>}
              </p>
              <p class="flow-desc">{s.desc}</p>
            </div>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ol>

    <p class="mono mt-5 text-xs leading-relaxed text-ink-faint">
      The coach follows the exact same two checks. Nothing it says to you gets to skip them.
    </p>
  </div>
</Section>
